cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HeatStressR, please cite it as below. Please also cite the original
  methodological reference for each heat-stress method used; see the corresponding
  function documentation.
type: software
title: "HeatStressR: Calculate Heat Stress Indices"
abstract: >-
  Calculates heat-stress indices from meteorological observations using shared
  psychrometric calculations and consistent method-specific input handling.
  Methods include the physically based outdoor wet-bulb globe temperature model
  of Liljegren et al. (2008), wet-bulb temperature and heat-index calculations,
  and established closed-form heat-stress indices. Provides row-level diagnostics,
  configurable physical controls, vectorized batch processing, and optional
  parallel execution for the Liljegren method. An independently maintained fork
  of HeatStress; its Liljegren implementation is not a bitwise-compatible port
  of the original program.
